  "purpose": "v3 (design_notes.md 79.2): PTECT-aware edge selection -- BOTTOM edge is only allowed for a TAP column whose X position falls OUTSIDE PTECT's box (X<-800 or X>800), since only then does the straight vertical core-exit hop from a BOTTOM pin avoid cutting through PTECT (X -800..800, Y -800..-150). TAP0/TAP3 qualify (X~+-802..807); TAP1/TAP2 do not (well inside +-800) and are forced to TOP. This keeps wire length close to v1's unconstrained optimum while still eliminating every PTECT crossing (v2's blanket TOP-only rule pushed 2 legs' arc spans past a third of the ring, forcing 13 shared lanes and colliding with NEAR_R=913 -- not needed once the PTECT rule is applied precisely).",
